{
  "description": "Boundary and duplicate-collapsing coverage for keychain configuration: empty decryption-key list, a decryption key identical to the encryption key (collapsed so the encryption key is never counted twice), repeated duplicate decryption keys, an empty-string encryption key rejected as a missing key, a missing encryption key with only decryption keys supplied, and various distinct encryption keys re-serialized to canonical form.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "input": {
        "op": "configure_keys",
        "encryptionKey": "k1.aesgcm256.DbQoar8ZLuUsOHZNyrnjlskInHDYlzF3q6y1KGM7DUM=",
        "decryptionKeys": []
      },
      "expected_output": "encryptionKey=k1.aesgcm256.DbQoar8ZLuUsOHZNyrnjlskInHDYlzF3q6y1KGM7DUM=\nencryptionKeyInKeychain=true\nkeychainSize=1\n"
    },
    {
